    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "Summary of the Mental Health Care Act, 2017\n•\tAct Name: The Mental Healthcare Act, 2017\n•\tExtent: Whole of India\n•\tObjective: Provide mental healthcare and services, protect, promote, and fulfill the rights of persons with mental illness, with a structured governance framework.\nGovernance & Decision Making\n•\tCentral Mental Health Authority (CMHA) & State Mental Health Authorities: Oversee mental healthcare, register establishments, and set norms. Decision Making: Authorities may have a presiding member with a second or casting vote to ensure decisive governance.\n•\tMental Health Review Boards (MHRBs): Review admissions, treatments, and decisions, ensuring patient rights.\nKey Provisions\n•\tAdvance Directives: Allowed for mental healthcare decisions.\n•\tNominated Representatives: Can be appointed for decision-making in the patient's best interest.\n•\tEmergency Treatment: Permitted without consent in life-threatening situations, with strict limitations.\n•\tProhibited Procedures: Electro-convulsive therapy without anesthesia, for minors, and psychosurgery without consent and Board approval.\nPenalties & Protections\n•\tPenalties: For unauthorized mental health establishments and violations.\n•\tProtection of Action Taken in Good Faith: For professionals acting in good faith.\n•\tOverriding Effect: This Act supersedes conflicting laws.",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
